 """Data model stations and links, see https://flatland-association.github.io/flatland-book/environment/environment/stations_links.html
 Convention: use fully qualified names.
+
+Conventions on the grid:
+
+- A node (`Pin.node`, `StoppingPoint.node`) and an edge (`Station.edges`, `Fibre.edges`) is a cell `(row, column)`,
+  row 0 at the top, column 0 on the left: the resource a train occupies, without a direction. It is not a node of
+  `GraphTransitionMap`, which is a cell entered in a direction, `(row, column, direction)`; a graph node belongs to a
+  station, stopping point or pin when its cell does, in every direction.
+- Directions are `Grid4TransitionsEnum`: N=0, E=1, S=2, W=3, N up (row - 1).
+- A gate's key is the side of the station its pins lie on, which is also the direction of a train leaving the station
+  through it: `N`, `E`, `S`, `W`, or `N1`, `N2`, ... along that side when it has several gates. Its pins are numbered
+  from 0.
+- Everything grid-specific beyond cells and gate keys is in `Station.grid`, so a non-grid producer can leave it out.
 """
